        <div id="skip-both" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            14. Who Should Skip Both?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Skip both if you have a milk allergy, eat vegan, or want an unflavored or unsweetened whey. Both are milk-based blends with artificial sweeteners and flavors, so neither suits a dairy-free diet or someone avoiding sweeteners entirely.
          </p>

          <p>
            Also skip both if you are very lactose intolerant. Ghost's lactase may help mild cases, but both contain whey concentrate, and a pure whey isolate or a plant protein will be gentler. Drug-tested athletes who want a flavor not on NSF's list should skip both brands' uncertified flavors and pick a certified product.
          </p>

          <p>
            Finally, if you want the lowest possible cost per gram and do not care about brand, store brands and bulk unflavored whey often beat both. Our <a href='/protein-powder-comparison/'>protein powder comparison</a> lets you sort every product we have checked by cost per 25 g.
