          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Comparing protein per scoop instead of per gram</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Ghost's 25 g looks bigger than Gold Standard's 24 g, but Ghost's scoop is 4 g heavier. Per gram of powder Gold Standard carries more protein, about 77% against 71%. Compare protein by weight, or cost per 25 g, before treating the bigger number on the front of the tub as the better deal.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming every Gold Standard flavor is NSF certified</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                The NSF Certified for Sport listing we checked names Double Rich Chocolate and Vanilla Ice Cream, not the whole range. If you are drug tested and want Cookies and Cream or Mocha Cappuccino, look up that exact flavor in the NSF database first. Brand-level banned-substance claims are not the same as a named certification.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying the small Gold Standard tub to save money</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Gold Standard is only cheaper than Ghost in the large tubs. At ON's own store price for the 1.98 lb tub, it came to about $2.68 per 25 g, more than Ghost's $2.12. Work out cost per 25 g for the size you are actually buying, because the value case depends on it.
              </p>
